  2026-10-02, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/accel/tcg/translator.c: UC_HOOK_BLOCK_ICOUNT leaves out the exit
    that ends a block, an until address or a uc_ctl exit inside it, which
    executes no instruction. Upstream counts it.
  - tests/unit/test_ctl.c: added test_block_icount_hook_until_mid_block and
    test_block_icount_hook_until_mid_block_arm.
  - include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c, qemu/tcg/tcg-op.c,
    qemu/target/arm/translate.c, translate.h, internals.h, helper.h,
    op_helper.c, qemu/arm.h, qemu/aarch64.h, symbols.sh: added
    UC_CTL_UC_USE_EXIT_AFTER_INSN, off by default, and
    UC_CTL_UC_EXIT_AFTER_INSN, which a memory callback calls to stop once the
    A32 or T32 instruction being executed completes, with pc on the next
    instruction, after the IT block inside one. Upstream can only stop with
    pc on the access instruction, which a resume runs again.
  - bindings/: regenerated the unicorn_const files of the dotnet, go, java,
    pascal, python, ruby and zig bindings with the two new control ids.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added the test_arm_exit_after_insn tests.
  2026-10-11, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c: store_helper refills a TLB entry that a
    UC_HOOK_MEM_WRITE callback emptied, as load_helper does after the read
    hooks. Upstream stores through the emptied entry.
  - qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c, qemu/include/tcg/tcg.h, uc.c: a TLB entry is
    flagged TLB_WATCHPOINT for reads or writes when a UC_HOOK_MEM_READ,
    UC_HOOK_MEM_READ_AFTER or UC_HOOK_MEM_WRITE hook covers its page, the
    backends no longer send every access to the slow path when such a hook
    exists, and adding or deleting such a hook flushes the TLB. Upstream
    sends every guest load and store to the slow path whenever any of these
    hooks exists, and a hook added after a block was translated misses that
    block's accesses.
  - include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c, symbols.sh,
    qemu/softmmu/memory.c, qemu/include/exec/memory.h, qemu/unicorn_common.h,
    the per-architecture symbol headers in qemu/, qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c:
    added uc_mem_map_alias(), a second window over a whole mapped region that
    shares its storage and RAMBlock with its own permissions, so a store
    through any window invalidates code translated through any other, also
    through a window the guest maps execute-never. Partial
    aliases, protection changes and memory snapshots over aliased memory are
    refused. Upstream has no alias mapping, and code translated through one
    uc_mem_map_ptr window survives a store through another over the same host
    memory.
  - include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c,
    qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c: added UC_CTL_UC_SLOW_PATH_COUNT, a count of data
    accesses that reached the slow path on a RAM page, for tests.
  - tests/unit/test_mem.c: added test_mem_write_hook_flush_tlb, the
    test_mem_hook tests, the test_mem_alias tests and the test_mem_slow_path
    tests.
  2026-10-16, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/target/arm/helper.c, include/unicorn/unicorn.h,
    include/unicorn/arm.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c: re-enabled the v8-M
    security attribution lookup through the SAU, with v8m_is_sau_exempt from
    upstream QEMU, and replaced its IDAU call by a host callback set with
    UC_CTL_ARM_IDAU. Added UC_CTL_ARM_SECURITY, off by default, which turns
    the lookup on. Upstream compiles the lookup out, so every address of a
    core with the Security Extension is Secure.
  - include/unicorn/arm.h, qemu/target/arm/unicorn_arm.c, internals.h,
    m_helper.c, qemu/arm.h, qemu/aarch64.h, symbols.sh: added host access to
    the v8-M security state, UC_ARM_REG_SECURE, the SAU registers SAU_CTRL,
    SAU_RNR, SAU_RBAR and SAU_RLAR, the FP context registers CPACR_S,
    CPACR_NS, FPCCR_S and FPCCR_NS, NSACR, the special registers MSP, PSP,
    CONTROL, PRIMASK, BASEPRI, FAULTMASK, MSPLIM and PSPLIM of each security
    state with the suffixes _S and _NS, and the read-only abort status and
    address FAULT_STATUS and FAULT_ADDRESS. A SECURE write switches the
    security state and its stack pointer banks, an SAU write flushes the
    TLB. Upstream has no register id for them.
  - include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c,
    qemu/softmmu/memory.c, qemu/include/exec/memory.h,
    qemu/unicorn_common.h, qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c: added
    uc_mmio_map_attrs, MMIO callbacks that receive the security and
    privilege attributes of each access, uc_mem_read_attrs and
    uc_mem_write_attrs, host accesses with given attributes, and
    UC_CTL_UC_REFUSE_MMIO, with which such a callback refuses the access it
    serves, raising a precise data abort. Upstream passes no attributes to
    MMIO callbacks and completes every access.
  - qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c, qemu/target/arm/tlb_helper.c, cpu.c,
    qemu/include/exec/cpu-defs.h, qemu/include/hw/core/cpu.h,
    include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c: added
    uc_ctl_bus_filter, ARM only, a host policy asked at each TLB fill of a
    RAM page. Its verdict sends the page's data accesses to a host callback,
    which allows them, reads them as zero and drops stores, or faults them,
    and can deny instruction fetches from the page. Upstream sends RAM
    accesses to no host callback but memory hooks.
  - qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c: uc_ctl_remove_cache finds the RAM
    address of an M-profile range through the address space, with no fetch
    TLB fill. Upstream fills the fetch TLB in the current security state,
    which faults and removes nothing for a range that state cannot fetch.
  - bindings/: regenerated the constant files of the dotnet, go, java,
    pascal, python, ruby and zig bindings with the new ids, and with
    UC_HOOK_BLOCK_ICOUNT and UC_CTL_UC_SLOW_PATH_COUNT, which they lacked.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added the test_arm_v8m tests, the bus filter
    tests, the attribute MMIO tests and the test_arm_mmio_refuse tests.
  2026-10-17, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/target/arm/helper.c, qemu/target/arm/unicorn_arm.c: a Non-secure
    FP instruction with NSACR.CP10 clear raises a NOCP UsageFault to Secure
    state, and a UC_ARM_REG_NSACR write rebuilds the hflags. Upstream runs
    the instruction on the Secure FP registers.
  - qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c, cpu-exec.c, cputlb.c,
    qemu/target/arm/translate.c, translate.h, tlb_helper.c, helper.c,
    internals.h, qemu/include/exec/exec-all.h, cpu-defs.h,
    qemu/include/tcg/tcg.h, the per-architecture symbol headers in qemu/,
    symbols.sh, include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h: a code page
    split by a small SAU region or by a bus filter verdict is translated by
    fetch window, the run of addresses that share one fetch verdict. A
    block that runs past its window end or into a page with no cached code
    runs once and is not cached. A fetch generation bumped by each TLB
    flush retires the blocks of split pages at their next lookup. Added the
    bus filter verdict UC_BUS_FETCH_EACH and the UC_BUS_FETCH_WINDOW()
    field. Upstream translates past an SAU region boundary inside a page
    and raises the fetch fault of the instruction past it at the first
    instruction of the block.
  - qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c: the bus filter judges a load before its
    UC_HOOK_MEM_READ hooks, and the load and store helpers look their TLB
    entry up again after a memory hook callback ran. Upstream keeps the
    entry pointer across the hooks, which a hook that flushes and resizes
    the TLB leaves pointing into freed memory.
  - qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c, translate-all.c, qemu/exec.c,
    qemu/softmmu/memory.c, qemu/target/arm/helper.c, tlb_helper.c,
    qemu/unicorn_common.h, qemu/include/qemu/compiler.h: placed the TLB
    fill path in a .text.hot.qemu section on ELF targets, and moved the bus
    filter's store value out of the store_helper frame, which keeps the
    stack protector off store_helper.
  - include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c,
    qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c: added the read-only
    UC_CTL_TB_TRANSLATIONS and UC_CTL_TB_FLUSHES, counts of translated
    blocks and of translation buffer flushes, for tests. Documented that
    IDAU regions cover whole TLB pages and that a host which changes a
    fetch verdict, a fetch window or the SAU from a callback ends the run
    after the change.
  - bindings/const_generator.py: skips function-like macros.
  - bindings/: regenerated the constant files of the seven bindings with
    the new ids.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added the split page, fetch-each, straddle,
    read hook flush and translation count tests.
  2026-10-18, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c: moved the bus filter's load value out of the
    load_helper frame, and built load_helper without the stack protector
    when UC_LOAD_HELPER_NO_STACK_PROTECTOR is defined.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added test_arm_read_hook_flush_resize and
    test_arm_bus_filter_read_hook_installs.
  2026-10-22, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c, translate-all.c, translate-all.h: a store to
